    "notes": "NVIDIA DGX Spark (ASUS Ascent GX10, GB10) on Ubuntu 24.04 / DGX OS, driver 580.173.02, CUDA 13.0. Same server as the prefix-caching-on cell on this machine (vLLM 0.27.1, stock vllm/vllm-openai:v0.27.1-aarch64 with transformers pinned to 5.8.1, TRITON_ATTN forced by Gemma 4 heterogeneous head dimensions, thinking off by chat-template default), with one change: --no-enable-prefix-caching. This cell exists because the prefill and needle workloads reuse prompts, so with vLLM's default prefix caching on they measure cache hits rather than prefill: on this machine prefill-8k returned 1057ms cold and 68ms warm for the same prompt, and all six longctx-needle-32k retrievals were cache hits. These numbers are cold prefill. The DeepSeek-v4-Flash service normally resident on this machine was stopped for the duration of the run."
